WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.070
John: Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday. I'm
actually at a minigolf course. I wish you

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:06.830
were here but you're busy, like, interviewing
the President or whatever. Oh wait.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.450
Hank: I'm in Florida where this happens.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.639
J: It's Question Tuesday, the day that we
answer real questions from real Nerdfighters

00:00:13.639 --> 00:00:17.140
while also playing minigolf. Are you nervous
about interviewing the President of the United

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.140
States?

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.380
H: Thanks for bringing it up.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.380
J: Are you?

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.380
H: Yes. I'm trying to golf.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.350
J: But is it going to affect your golfing?

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.220
John and Hank's mother: It absolutely is.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.220
H: Apparently.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.220
Mom: Oh.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.050
J: Oh, oh, oh, oh! That was terrible. Why
do you look so much taller than me? It must

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.280
be because there's something wrong with the
ground. Anyway, what's your favorite flightless

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.280
bird?

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.280
H: You're my favorite brother.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.891
J: Hank just got a hole in one, but I insisted
that he tapped it twice because I don't want

00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:44.010
to get too far behind and I'm the big brother
and that's how we compete. I may not be better

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.610
than you, Hank, but I am able to change the
rules mid-stream. Are you behind me?

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:48.660
H: What are you...

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.060
J: Nothing. There's a ton of waterfalls in
this joint. If your last name were any other

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.710
color what would it be?

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:56.020
H: Oh, chartreuse.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:02.130
J: (Laughs) I would go with blue which I think
is a kind of chartreuse. The next question

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:06.140
is will you try on each other's glasses and
I think we should do that and putt-putt.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.140
H: Ooh.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.600
J: Hank's prescription is actually pretty
close to mine. I feel fairly comfortable.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.250
H: Yours are just mostly dirty. Oh my God,
John. I don't clean my glasses very often

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.250
but that's just disgusting.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:20.720
J: Can he perform under the pressure of wearing
his brother's glasses? It's Hank Green, it's

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.240
Hank Green! Oh no!

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.760
H: There it is. Werdegerdeh.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.110
J: Oh, Oh! Come on! Give me that bounce!

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.110
H: That was a good bounce.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.180
J: Between the two of us, who was weirder
in high school?

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.080
H: Oh, I don't know. me? I feel like me. You
had all those friends.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.630
J: Who's better at rhyming?

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:44.880
H: I don't know but I have pretty good timing.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:51.759
J: Sorry, I was trying to think of a rhyme
for timing. I didn't get there. Diming? Fliming?

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:57.229
Climbing! Goh, it took me a minute. Hank might
be better. Who's your favorite member of One

00:01:57.229 --> 00:01:58.229
Direction?

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:01.000
H: Let's go with the police officer guy.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.850
J: I like the construction worker, you know.

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:03.850
H: Yeah. I feel it.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.590
J: They're all good though. I love that song.

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:06.659
H: Yeah.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:10.590
H &amp; J: "YMCA. It's fun to stay at the YMCA."

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:13.250
J: What should win the Oscar for Best Picture?

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.209
H: I'm gonna go with The Fault In Our Stars,
John.

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:17.830
J: Not nominated. Um, I'm gonna go...

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.480
H: You look like the TFIOS clouds right now.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:24.090
J: I know, it's a... marketing. Never not
marketing. I'm gonna go with Whiplash or Selma.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.120
I thought that both those were excellent.
Hank, how do you feel about koalas?

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.120
H: They poop in their sleep.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.270
J: Is that true? Can you play the ukulele?

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.260
H: No. Yes, I can play, like, two chords.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.610
J: I can't play it at all. And what's your
favorite type of hummus?

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:37.610
H: Uh, chickpea.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.770
J: I didn't know there were types of hummus.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.319
H: It's the final hole and we are tied.

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:44.510
J: Oh, it's tense, very tense.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.510
H: Eighteen.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:48.280
J: Hank is significantly closer than I am.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.420
H: For the tie.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.500
J: No!

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:57.540
H: Oh! Oh, oh no! How does it feel to be less
good than me?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.890
J: I'll see you on Friday.

